        <h1 class="profile-detail-name">Muhammad</h1>
        <div class="info-stats" style="margin-top:10px;">
          <div class="info-stat"><span class="info-stat-label">Period</span><span class="info-stat-val">c. 570 CE – 632 CE</span></div>
          <div class="info-stat"><span class="info-stat-label">Born</span><span class="info-stat-val">c. 570 in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mecca">Mecca</a>, in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/banu-hashim">Banu Hashim</a> clan of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/quraysh">Quraysh</a>, son of Abdullah ibn Abd al-Muttalib and Amina bint Wahb</span></div>
          <div class="info-stat"><span class="info-stat-label">Died</span><span class="info-stat-val">8 June 632 in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/medina">Medina</a>, after an illness of some days; buried where he died, in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/aisha">Aisha</a>'s house, later included in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/prophets-mosque">Prophet's Mosque</a></span></div>
          <div class="info-stat"><span class="info-stat-label">Who they were</span><span class="info-stat-val">Founder of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/islam">Islam</a>; held by Muslims to be the Seal of the Prophets, the last prophet sent by God; leader of the Muslim community in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/medina">Medina</a> from 622 and of most of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/arabia">Arabia</a> by 632</span></div>
